flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a pull request picks the legs of the Variants
    accDescr: A pull request starts the job variants plan, and a run on a schedule, by hand or of the Next runner workflow runs every leg. A change of what every leg runs with, the workflow, Copier, its Python, copier.yml or the plan itself, runs every leg. Otherwise the plan renders the project of each leg from the merge commit and from main; a render that fails runs every leg. A project that differs, or an adopted leg whose answers change, runs its leg; a project that stays the same to the byte skips it, and its reason goes into the summary. The required check variants passes when each leg that ran passed and the plan passed.

    pr(["A pull request"])
    other(["A run on a schedule, by hand<br>or of the Next runner workflow"])
    files{"Does it change what<br>every leg runs with?"}
    render["The plan renders the project of each leg<br>from the merge commit and from main"]
    differs{"Does this project differ,<br>or the answers of this leg?"}
    every["Every leg runs"]
    leg["This leg runs"]
    skip["This leg doesn't run<br>the summary says why"]
    gate(["The check variants: the plan and<br>each leg that ran have passed"])

    pr --> files
    other --> every
    files -- "yes" --> every
    files -- "no" --> render
    render -- "a render fails" --> every
    render --> differs
    differs -- "yes" --> leg
    differs -- "no" --> skip
    every --> gate
    leg --> gate
    skip --> gate

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    class pr,other,render,every,leg bot
